subtasks.description:
Modify `internal/orchestrator/task_processing.go` to add the content-aware dedup check in `scheduleSubtasks()` BEFORE the `CanSpawn()` gate.

Insert the new check after the dependency check (line ~234) and before the existing `isWorkAlreadyMerged` check (line ~238). The new check handles the case where NO agent was previously assigned (new subtask IDs from replanning) but work already exists on the integration branch.

Code to add (after the dependency check, before `if sub.AssignedAgentID != nil`):

```go
// Content-aware dedup: check if this subtask's deliverables already
// exist on the integration branch, even without a prior agent assignment.
// This handles re-planning where new subtask IDs are created but prior
// agents' work was already merged.
if sub.AssignedAgentID == nil {
    estimatedFiles := getEstimatedFiles(sub)
    if len(estimatedFiles) > 0 {
        featureName := strings.TrimPrefix(parent.WorktreeBranch, "feature/")
        featureDir := o.worktree.FeatureWorktreePath(featureName)
        changedFiles, _ := worktree.GetChangedFiles(featureDir, o.worktree.DefaultBranch)
        if len(changedFiles) > 0 {
            commitMsgs, _ := getCommitMessages(featureDir, o.worktree.DefaultBranch)
            if HasExistingWork(estimatedFiles, changedFiles, commitMsgs, sub.Title) {
                o.logger.Info("schedule: content-aware dedup detected existing work, fast-tracking",
                    "subtask_id", sub.ID, "title", sub.Title)
                // Fast-track to done (same pattern as isWorkAlreadyMerged block below).
                transitions := []model.TaskStatus{
                    model.StatusPlanning,
                    model.StatusPlanReview,
                    model.StatusInProgress,
                    model.StatusTestingReady,
                    model.StatusMerging,
                    model.StatusDone,
                }
                for _, target := range transitions {
                    if sub.Status == target {
                        continue
                    }
                    evt, tErr := state.TransitionTask(sub, target, "orchestrator",
                        map[string]any{"reason": "content-aware-dedup"})
                    if tErr != nil {
                        continue
                    }
                    if err := o.db.Create(evt).Error; err != nil {
                        o.logger.Error("schedule: save dedup event", "subtask_id", sub.ID, "error", err)
                        break
                    }
                }
                if err := o.db.Save(sub).Error; err != nil {
                    o.logger.Error("schedule: save dedup subtask", "subtask_id", sub.ID, "error", err)
                }
                continue
            }
        }
    }
}
```

Constraints:
- task_processing.go is currently 690 lines; adding ~35 lines keeps it under 800
- Do NOT modify the existing `isWorkAlreadyMerged` block — it handles a different case (same agent ID, branch ancestry)
- Do NOT change function signatures
- Use gofmt formatting
- Verify: `go build ./internal/orchestrator/` and `go test ./internal/orchestrator/` pass
